# Documents - chapters, marklower prose, tables, and lists. Sources: CHAPTER.md,
# MARKLOWER.md - progress in ../../DOCSMIGRATION.md.
Documents
description: chapters and chunks, marklower prose, tables, and lists
- >
  A **document** in yamlover is a [chapter](*::documents:chapter): a readable page whose positional
  body interleaves prose, media, tables, lists, and subchapters. The prose format is
  [marklower](*::documents:marklower) - intentionally below Markdown: inline markup only, with
  structure delegated to yamlover nodes. Together they are the document layer built on the
  [language](*::language).
- >
  This chapter absorbs `CHAPTER.md` and `MARKLOWER.md`. Cross-links into the language point at the
  [model](*::language:model), [metadata](*::meta), [pointers](*::language:pointers),
  and [concretes](*::language:concretes).
- *: chapter
- *: marklower
